{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa and Marco's First Argument"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Girl With a Suitcase"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le12ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.</p> You use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> necessarily connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about experience. When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now.</p> For example:</br> <span class=\"strong\">I have learned</span> English = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.</br> <span class=\"strong\">He has bought</span> a painting = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the verb in Present Perfect sentences."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past participle form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">I have gone</span> to Japan.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lose\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lost\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"lost\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">He's lost</span> all sense of self.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"feel\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"felt\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"felt\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">I have never felt</span> so humiliated.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"decide\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"decided\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"decided\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">I've decided</span> I need a break.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to and Would to Talk About Past Habits"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the expressions <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span> to talk about events or activities that were usual or repetitive in the past. You may use them to describe past routines."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> with all types of verbs, including general condition or specific actions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I never used to behave like this.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You used <span class=\"strong\">would</span> when there is a specific time for the action to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<span class=\"italic\"> <br/>In San Francisco, I would play our reunion over and over in my head.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For the negative form of <span class=\"strong\">used to</span>, you use the auxiliary verb <span class=\"strong\">did</span>; the form is <span class=\"strong\">didn't use</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:<span class=\"italic\"> <br/>I <span class=\"strong\">didn't use</span> to behave like this.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pack"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put things in a suitcase or bag for a trip"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm in my bedroom, packing my suitcase."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use in an argument."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "humiliated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling embarrassed or ashamed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I've never felt so humiliated."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reunion"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when two or more people come together after a long period of time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would play our reunion over and over in my head."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le12ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "toiletries"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "things used to take care of your body (soap, shampoo etc.)"}, {"typ